WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:06.302
- [Voiceover] In 2010,
this man, Forrest Fenn

00:00:06.302 --> 00:00:09.498
hid a chest filled with
gold and rare artifacts

00:00:09.498 --> 00:00:11.812
somewhere in the Rocky Mountains.

00:00:11.812 --> 00:00:14.323
The search for this
million-dollar treasure

00:00:14.323 --> 00:00:17.783
has obsessed thousands
of seekers worldwide.

00:00:17.783 --> 00:00:21.046
And the trail starts with
this poem, which Fenn wrote.

00:00:21.046 --> 00:00:23.369
It contains nine clues that point

00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:25.306
to the treasure's location.

00:00:25.306 --> 00:00:27.347
- It's here someplace.

00:00:27.347 --> 00:00:28.597
Are we rolling?

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.442
As I have gone alone in there

00:00:32.442 --> 00:00:34.528
and with my treasures bold,

00:00:34.528 --> 00:00:36.624
I can keep my secret where

00:00:36.624 --> 00:00:39.207
and hint of riches new and old.

00:00:46.427 --> 00:00:48.563
- [Voiceover] Fenn's motivation
for hiding the treasure

00:00:48.563 --> 00:00:51.637
was to give hope to those
knocked down by the recession

00:00:51.637 --> 00:00:54.955
and to inspire them to explore the wild.

00:00:54.955 --> 00:00:58.839
- I found a beautiful little
Romanesque treasure chest

00:00:58.839 --> 00:01:01.662
and I started filling
it up with gold coins

00:01:01.662 --> 00:01:05.031
and gold nuggets and
about 200 native rubies.

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:06.586
There are two ceylon sapphires,

00:01:06.586 --> 00:01:09.512
there are eight emeralds,
a bunch of diamonds.

00:01:09.512 --> 00:01:10.845
But mostly gold.

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:12.715
I don't know what it's worth

00:01:12.715 --> 00:01:14.951
and I don't even want to think about that.

00:01:14.951 --> 00:01:16.365
You're not gonna be disappointed

00:01:16.365 --> 00:01:18.906
if you find that treasure chest.

00:01:18.906 --> 00:01:22.856
(melodious piano music)

00:01:22.856 --> 00:01:27.023
- I am Cynthia Meachum and I
am a full-time treasure hunter.

00:01:27.953 --> 00:01:31.106
I have been looking
for Fenn's treasure now

00:01:31.106 --> 00:01:34.523
for a little over three and a half years.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.761
- I hid the treasure chest more than

00:01:37.761 --> 00:01:40.815
8.25 miles north of Santa Fe,

00:01:40.815 --> 00:01:43.501
in the Rocky Mountains some place.

00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:45.168
Nobody knows but me.

00:01:48.624 --> 00:01:51.311
- In the poem that you have
to solve, Forrest always said,

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:53.679
you have to find where warm waters halt

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:57.096
and to me this is where warm waters halt.

00:01:58.424 --> 00:02:02.591
That's where I think we need
to find the treasure chest.

00:02:03.899 --> 00:02:05.857
- [Voiceover] The thrill of
this chase for Fenn's treasure

00:02:05.857 --> 00:02:08.712
has led many to leave the
safety of known trails

00:02:08.712 --> 00:02:10.545
and well-beaten paths.

00:02:12.717 --> 00:02:16.106
- The mountains are very unforgiving.

00:02:16.106 --> 00:02:19.263
It's extremely important that
you know what you're doing

00:02:19.263 --> 00:02:22.326
and you know where you're going.

00:02:22.326 --> 00:02:26.076
You can end up in big
trouble really quickly.

00:02:27.308 --> 00:02:30.030
There's even one hiker that's been lost

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:34.197
looking for the treasure and
he hasn't been found yet.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:38.824
- [Voiceover] To Fenn's knowledge,

00:02:38.824 --> 00:02:41.307
the treasure remains a hidden mystery.

00:02:41.307 --> 00:02:44.957
But the real reward
should come from the hunt.

00:02:44.957 --> 00:02:48.163
- I was positive this
was our warm waters halt

00:02:48.163 --> 00:02:51.056
and unfortunately I don't think

00:02:51.056 --> 00:02:54.354
that this is gonna be the spot.

00:02:54.354 --> 00:02:57.162
It doesn't matter what
state you treasure-hunt in,

00:02:57.162 --> 00:03:00.212
you gonna have beautiful
scenery like this.

00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:03.451
And it doesn't matter if you
find the treasure chest or not,

00:03:03.451 --> 00:03:05.389
this is finding the treasure.

00:03:05.389 --> 00:03:06.306
Right here.

00:03:09.282 --> 00:03:11.341
- So hear me all and listen good,

00:03:11.341 --> 00:03:13.506
your effort will be worth the cold.

00:03:13.506 --> 00:03:15.940
If you are brave and in the wood,

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:18.675
I give you title to the gold.

00:03:18.675 --> 00:03:21.592
(soft piano music)

